v3.0.0 - 2026-11-16
-------------------
  * parse() doesn't modify the line: it parses a copy in the new
    logdata field linebuf, takes a const char *, reads only the
    first len bytes, and the line doesn't have to be terminated
    (before it wrote a '\0' to line[len], which changed the script
    strings in the bindings, and crashed PHP with opcache)
  * A line of 8192 (MSCLOG_LINE_BUFF_SIZE) bytes or longer (without
    the line ending) isn't parsed, it's reported as an error, and
    entry_is_modsecline is set if it's a ModSecurity line
  * Fix: the fields are searched only in the ModSecurity part of the
    line, before the context of the web server (Nginx: client,
    server, request, host, referrer; Apache: referer): fake fields
    there replaced the real [file], [id], [msg], [hostname],
    [unique_id], ...; the end of the ModSecurity part is the context
    right after its last field (with an optional ' while ACTION' on
    Nginx), if there are more such places (a fake one), or the only
    one is followed by fields on an Apache line or a line cut by
    Nginx (the real context can be missing there), the fields
    aren't used (only the class and the message are kept), and an
    error is reported - also if the ModSecurity part contains more
    than one [file] or [id]; Nginx log_client and log_server are used
    if their part is right after the ModSecurity part, even if fake
    ones follow it (or the only one after the message of a line
    without fields), otherwise a warning says why
  * Fix: [uri] and [unique_id] are searched after [hostname], not
    from the beginning of the line (a '[uri "' in the message
    replaced the real [uri]); if the ModSecurity part contains more
    '[hostname "' or '[uri "' (libmodsecurity3 doesn't escape the '"'
    in them), the line is broken, and the two values aren't used
  * Fix: the class of an Apache line ("Warning.", "Access", "Rule",
    "Request body", "Audit log") is taken only from the start of the
    message (it was found anywhere, eg. in the [uri]), and [client]
    or [remote] only from the prefix, before " ModSecurity:"
  * Fix: log_modsec_msg_length of the Apache "Request body" and
    "Audit log" lines (it was 0)
  * Fix: an empty Nginx [hostname] is taken from the ', host: "' of
    the context only if there is exactly one (a 'host: "' in the
    request line won before), otherwise the line is broken; without a
    context (eg. a cut line) it's not searched at all
  * parse() initializes the logdata: the caller doesn't have to
    clear it before every line, the bindings don't clear it anymore
  * Fix: don't store a part of a UTF-8 character when a field is
    cut, and don't trim a value that isn't cut
  * Fix: quadratic re-search in find_pattern() on lines with many
    partial field names
  * Bindings: if len is bigger than the line, the whole line is
    parsed, and an error is added to log_entry_errors (by the new
    parse_checked() of the library); a negative len raises an error
  * A line with a NUL character (except at its end) isn't parsed,
    it's reported as an error, like a too long line; the Python and
    Ruby bindings don't raise an error for it anymore, so all four
    bindings handle it the same way
  * parse() reports an unknown log type as an error, the bindings
    raise an error for it
  * Python binding: fix reference leaks, report the real argument
    errors, accept the line as bytes (the values and the error
    messages are bytes too),
    build with setuptools instead of distutils
  * Ruby binding: parse() and the constants are in the
    MscRubyLogParser module (API change), new entry_is_modsecline,
    the values get the encoding of the line (binary if it isn't ASCII
    compatible, eg. UTF-16), the pointer of the line
    is taken after the conversions of the arguments (a to_int could
    free its buffer)
  * Lua binding: new entry_is_broken, the constants are integers
  * PHP binding: fix the TSRM cache macro of ZTS builds, remove
    unused variables, the version of the module is MODULE_VERSION
    (phpversion() said 1.0)
  * Python and Ruby test scripts pass the length in bytes
  * The installed header compiles as ISO C90 (no // comments), make
    check tests it
  * README: the C sample reads lines up to 2 * MSCLOG_LINE_BUFF_SIZE
  * examples/example01.c doesn't clear logdata for every line, and
    reads lines up to 2 * MSCLOG_LINE_BUFF_SIZE (a longer line was cut
    into more records at 4096 bytes), and it's built with the header
    of the source tree (a VPATH build, eg. make distcheck, used an
    installed one)
  * pkg-config file: the version and the paths come from configure
    (it said 0.3.0, and had a fixed libdir)
  * Build: the version is only in src/msclogparser.h: configure
    (package version, pkg-config, SONAME), the Python package and the
    MODULE_VERSION of the bindings take it from there
  * Build: make uninstall removes the bindings (the Python module
    from the site directories of the interpreter, the module is
    installed with its pip), and make install of the Lua, Ruby and
    PHP bindings honors DESTDIR
  * Build: make doesn't rerun the autotools (AM_MAINTAINER_MODE), the
    committed generated files are used; run autoreconf -fi after a
    change of configure.ac or a Makefile.am
  * ABI change: logdata has a new field, the SONAME is
    libmsclogparser.so.3, rebuild the bindings and applications

v2.0.0 - 2026-11-03
-------------------
  * New field: log_server, the server_name of the Nginx server
    block that served the request
  * Nginx log_client and log_server are used only if the line
    contains exactly one ", client: ADDR, server: NAME" part,
    and isn't cut by Nginx (a client can send a fake one)
  * Fix: Rule error lines fill log_rule_id, log_rule_file and
    log_rule_line
  * Bounds checks on the stack buffers and the data/error pools,
    the truncated fields get an error message
  * Fix possible crash if the operand of an Apache "Warning."
    message contains ". "
  * Align the error positions in the error pool
  * Remove the CR of a CRLF line ending too
  * Ruby binding: return every rule tag, not only the first
  * Build: "./configure && make" without any binding doesn't run
    make endlessly in bindings/
  * Tests: make check
  * ABI change: logdata has a new field, the SONAME is
    libmsclogparser.so.2, rebuild the bindings and applications

v1.0.1 - 2026-08.14
-------------------
  * Fix possible segfault if the "Warning. ..." message is too
    long in apache's error.log

v1.0.0 - 2026-06-17
-------------------
  * The C structure of the structure library has been
    reorganized, most fields are now accessible via indexed arrays.
  * Some code cleanups

v0.3.0 - 2026-01-19
-------------------
  * Align fields to new format of Apache
    * remove 2nd [client] field lookup
    * add lookup for [remote] if [client] does not exist
  * Align fields to ne format of Apache
    * use [host] field for host if exists
  * Modernize Python3 module build
  * Add pkgconfig related files and entries
  * Replace pointer type to static in method
    of error storage
  * Add boundary check in parsing of log tail

v0.2.0 - 2024-06-21
-------------------
  * Get host from 'host' field in case of Nginx log
  * Increment possible length of [ver]; fix field name
  * URI field was truncated, fixed
  * Long lines caused segfault, fixed
  * Change fields name

v0.1.0 - 2023-02-11
-------------------
  * Initial release
